412: We first identify the actual relative square, before applying the
413: flop formula. Let \(f\) be the positive one-turn return on the
414: exterior of the single native star, using precisely the single
415: product following (DZ.8). Choose a global family connection
416: compatible with this product on its boundary. Its literal pullback
417: to the degree-two parameter cover has relative return \(f^2\):
418: the first sheet has endpoint \(f\), and the second uses the same
419: connection and boundary product under the transition \(E_v^{-1}\)
420: in (DZ.8a). The full forward arrows compose as
421: \((R_{\rm ord}^{(1)})^2=R_{\rm ord}^{(2)}\) and likewise on the
422: cap, by RG.3. Thus the closed parameter and cap square is exact.
423: 
424: The ordinary-product calculation (DZ.22), followed by the inverse
425: of the actual boundary change (DZ.23), computes this same
426: pulled-back native return. Indeed both resulting connections use
427: the literal native boundary product (DZ.8a); their interpolation
428: with that boundary fixed supplies a relative isotopy of endpoints.
429: Hence the native pair (DZ.24) is the free pair of \(f^2\).
430: K23's relative generators \(L,R\) commute literally, and its
431: disc-supported central factor is central. The free-coordinate
432: homomorphism to \(\mathbb Z^2\) consequently sends
433: \(f^2\) to twice the free coordinates of \(f\).
434: Multiplication by two is injective on each of these two integral
435: coordinates. We therefore obtain the actual single native pair
436: \[
437:                          (m(f),n(f))=(1-a,a).       \tag{DZ.26}
438: \]
439: This argument takes an actual square in the relative group and
440: uses its torsion-free coordinates. It does not divide a class in
441: \(\Theta_7\).
442: 
443: K23's already proved actual relative conjugation for the same
444: single-loop Cox map is
445: \[
446:  T(L^mR^n\mathcal C^s)T^{-1}
447:           =L^{-n}R^{m+2n}\mathcal C^{s+n}.
448: \]
449: Here the native central coordinate is the actual single return
450: \(s=[Z_{\mathcal T}]\), and the single Cox family arrow is the
451: one carried by (DZ.5) and (DZ.25). Applying the identity to
452: (DZ.26) proves
453: \[
454:                  [Z_{J\mathcal T}]-[Z_{\mathcal T}]
455:                          =a\quad\text{in }\mathbb Z/28. \tag{DZ.27}
456: \]
457: Every source/cap/scalar datum is the same one as RG.25. This
458: relation is derived from the actual single-loop relative
459: conjugation. Combining it with the already proved paired sum
460: still leaves a two-torsion ambiguity for either individual
461: source-zero class; neither is selected here.
462: 
463: ## DZ.5. The paired returns with their exact remaining ambiguity
464: 
465: Keep the actual paired sum of P3K.58, with its P3K.57 infinity
466: comparison. Write
467: \[
468:  A_{\rm scalar}=0\quad(a,b,m)=(1,2,4p),\qquad
469:  A_{\rm scalar}=1-3p\quad(a,b,m)=(2,1,4p-1).
470: \]
471: In both rows P3K.58 is exactly
472: \[
473:        [Z_{\mathcal T}]+[Z_{J\mathcal T}]
474:                           =-a+2kA_{\rm scalar}.
475: \]
476: Together with (DZ.27) it implies
477: \[
478:              2\bigl([Z_{J\mathcal T}]-kA_{\rm scalar}\bigr)=0
479:                               \quad\text{in }\mathbb Z/28.
480: \]
481: The kernel of multiplication by two in this specified group is
482: exactly \(\{0,14\}\): for an integer representative \(r\),
483: \(2r\equiv0\pmod{28}\) is equivalent to \(r\equiv0\pmod{14}\).
484: Consequently the actual pair has precisely the form
485: \[
486:  \boxed{\;
487:  ([Z_{\mathcal T}],[Z_{J\mathcal T}])
488:    =(-a+kA_{\rm scalar}+14e,\ kA_{\rm scalar}+14e),
489:        \qquad e\in\{0,1\}.\;}                       \tag{DZ.28}
490: \]
491: This is a determination of the two-element set allowed by the
492: proved sum and the actual single-loop flop morphism. No value of
493: \(e\) is selected. The common \(e\) belongs to the particular
494: retained family data; this proof makes no assertion that it is
495: constant across distinct norm or source data.
496: 
497: ## DZ.6. Scope and exact verification
498: 
499: DZ.27 concerns only the two stated initial/reflected fan objects,
500: the one III-star cap and the literal scalar \(v^{km}\lambda_0\).
501: The single endpoint \(q^{nk}\), its literal pullback
502: \(q^{2nk}\), their period reindexings, the bounded seam
503: multipliers, and the cap square have all been carried.
504: The earlier diagnostic's algebra is recovered, but its formerly
505: missing plumbing/seam map is now (DZ.5)--(DZ.14), with the actual
506: single-to-double square in DZ.4.
507: All symbolic chart, seam, quaternion-exponent, trace and pair
508: identities are checked in
509: \path{code/part3/source_zero_double_loop_product.py}.
510: The complete geometric proof has passed the independent checks and
511: root audits, including the literal pullback and actual relative square.
512: The scalar \(C_1\) consistency diagnostic
513: is separate and is not used to extend this exact \(C_2\) comparison.
